      },
      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "Text::CSV_XS versions before 1.65 for Perl leak the parsed fields of a record that fails to parse in getline.\n\ngetline collects the fields of a record into a new array and returns a reference to it only when the parse succeeds. When the record has a syntax error, getline returns undef and never frees the array or the fields parsed before the error.\n\nA long-running process parsing untrusted CSV retains every malformed record it is sent, so repeated malformed input exhausts its memory.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
